rule ROUTE102 "debug-server-exposed" {
  lang python
  severity error

  find c: call where c.callee.name == "run" and c.text ~ /\.run\(.*debug\s*=\s*True/
  report c "the web server starts with debug=True: the interactive debugger is reachable over HTTP"

  example fire python """
    app.run(host="0.0.0.0", debug=True)  #~ error
  """
  example clean python """
    app.run(host="127.0.0.1", debug=False)
  """
  example notapplicable markdown """
    Prose starts no server.
  """
  explain """
    Flask-style frameworks answer debug=True with a console that executes code for any client that can reach the port. The check reads Flask-style `run(...)` calls; other frameworks and languages need an adapter and are reported Unresolved by the family, never clean.
    ## Remedy
    Drop `debug=True` and read the flag from configuration that is off in production.
  """
}
